.TH PASTE 1 "2026" "spicule" "spicule User Commands"
.SH NAME
paste \- merge corresponding or consecutive lines of files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B paste
.RB [ \-s ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR list ]
.I file
.RI [ file ]\ .\|.\|.
.SH DESCRIPTION
By default,
.B paste
concatenates the corresponding lines of every
.I file
operand: for each output row, one line is read from each file and
joined into a single output line, replacing every newline except the
last with a delimiter character. Once a file runs out of lines, it
contributes an empty field for every remaining output row \(em the
merge does not stop until every file has reached end\-of\-file.
.PP
At least one
.I file
operand is required;
.B paste
with no operands at all is a usage error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-d " list"
Use the characters of
.I list
in place of the default \fI<tab>\fR as the delimiter between merged
fields, one character per field boundary, reused circularly from the
beginning of
.I list
once it is exhausted.
.I list
may contain the backslash escapes
.BR \en " (newline), " \et " (tab), and " \e\e " (a literal backslash);"
any other backslash sequence is a usage error, as is an empty
.IR list .
.TP
.B \-s
Serial mode: instead of merging corresponding lines across files,
concatenate every line of one file at a time onto a single output
row, delimited the same way, writing one output row per
.I file
operand in the order given.
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I file
A pathname of an input file. If
.B \-
is given, standard input is used. A file that cannot be opened is
diagnosed and thereafter treated as permanently empty \(em it
contributes only empty fields in parallel mode, or a single empty
output row in serial mode \(em while the rest of the files given
continue to be merged normally.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All input files were merged successfully.
.TP
.B 1
One or more files could not be opened (the files that did open were
still merged), or a memory allocation failed.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error: an invalid option, no
.I file
operand at all, or an invalid
.I list
argument to
.BR \-d .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cut (1),
.BR tr (1),
.BR wc (1)
